    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <FlexiPage> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
         matching parent xml file" error.

         2026-08-28 — Dynamic Actions was enabled on this page in App Builder (retrieved with
         enableActionsConfiguration / enableActionsInNative already flipped true -> true, and an
         `actionNames` property present with ZERO <valueListItems> in the whole file). This is the
         repo-documented "enabling Dynamic Actions with an empty actionNames property silently
         discards every inherited action" failure — the page rendered NO action buttons at all
         (not even Edit) until this change. This finishes the work commit 95557f5 (2026-08-27)
         explicitly deferred for Transaction__c because it had no Dynamic Actions to populate at
         the time.

         🔴 AMENDED 2026-08-28, SAME DAY, AFTER A FAILED DEPLOY (0Afiw000000SstVCAS). THIS BLOCK
         USED TO SAY "THE TEN ENTRIES ADDED BELOW restore the bar" AND LISTED SIX NON-STAGE
         ENTRIES (Edit, Clone, Delete, LogACall, NewEvent, NewTask) AS ADDED HERE ALONGSIDE THE
         FOUR STAGE ACTIONS. THAT WAS WRONG AND IS CORRECTED, NOT LEFT STANDING. The deploy failed
         with "Component [force:highlightsPanel] attribute [actionNames]: We couldn't validate
         Action LogACall" — the highlightsPanel's actionNames attribute does not validate a
         standard button or a global quick action, only object-specific custom quick actions. Every
         other already-deployed record page in this repo (Opportunity_Record_Page,
         Disposition_Record_Page, NDA_Record_Page, LOI_Record_Page, Underwriting_Record_Page) lists
         ONLY <Object>.<CustomAction> entries — not one of them carries Edit/Clone/Delete or a
         global action. This page now matches that precedent exactly.

         ⇒ actionNames BELOW HOLDS EXACTLY FOUR ENTRIES, the named per-hop stage actions —
         Transaction__c.Move_to_Due_Diligence / Move_to_Closing_Prep / Move_to_Post_Closing /
         Move_to_Closed_Won, one per hop of RecordStageAdvanceService.TRANSACTION_NEXT_STAGE — each
         gated on BOTH {!$Permission.CustomPermission.Transaction_Stage_Actions} EQUAL true (the
         same gate TransactionActionPermissionService / RecordStageAdvanceService already enforce
         server-side for this object) AND {!Record.Stage__c} EQUAL its own SOURCE stage, so exactly
         one (or zero, at the 'Closed Won' terminal) renders per record. Transaction__c.Advance_Stage
         — the generic button these four named actions replace — is REMOVED from both this page and
         the layout's platformActionList in the same change; the quickAction file itself is not
         deleted, matching the retirement convention used for NDA__c/LOI__c/Underwriting__c etc.

         🔴 THE SIX NON-STAGE ACTIONS (Edit, Clone, Delete, LogACall, NewEvent, NewTask) ARE
         DELIBERATELY *NOT* RE-LISTED HERE, AND THAT IS A REAL, ACCEPTED, BEHAVIOURAL CONSEQUENCE OF
         ENABLING DYNAMIC ACTIONS — NOT AN OVERSIGHT THIS COMMIT INTRODUCES. Before Dynamic Actions
         was enabled on this page (a change made in App Builder, outside this commit), those six
         actions rendered on the Transaction highlights panel via the layout's platformActionList
         fallback. Once Dynamic Actions is on, that fallback no longer applies, and the
         highlightsPanel's actionNames attribute cannot carry them at all (see the failed-deploy
         error above) — so THEY ARE GONE FROM THE HIGHLIGHTS PANEL, full stop, on every one of the
         five sibling pages already deployed this way and now on this one too. A user who wants to
         Edit, Clone, Delete, Log a Call, create a New Event or New Task on a Transaction must use a
         different entry point (the object's standard buttons/menu elsewhere on the page, or the
         Activity panel for the three activity actions) — this was seen and accepted when Dynamic
         Actions was turned on, not missed by this change.

         🔴 Transaction__c CARRIES NO RECORD TYPES (verified: no <recordTypes> element in
         objects/Transaction__c/Transaction__c.object-meta.xml, no recordTypes/ folder), so none
         of the four stage entries below needs a record-type criterion — this page's shape follows
         Underwriting_Record_Page's single-sequence pattern, not NDA_Record_Page's dual-type one.

         🔴 THE GATE IS Transaction_Stage_Actions, NOT Acquisition_Deal_Actions. Every other
         object's per-stage entries in this repo are AND-ed with Acquisition_Deal_Actions or
         Disposition_Deal_Actions — Transaction__c has its OWN custom permission
         (customPermissions/Transaction_Stage_Actions.customPermission-meta.xml), already wired
         into TransactionActionPermissionService via FeatureManagement.checkPermission and granted
         through the LAYER-4 Transaction_Stage_Actions_Access set (member of DPEG_Transaction_Team)
         — see that service's header for why a layer-4 grant is correct here specifically and does
         not generalise to the other two gates. No permission set changes ship with this page edit;
         the token and its grantees already exist.

         ⚠ Nothing else gates the move to 'Closed Won'. Transaction_Complete_Close.flow-meta.xml
         fires off Transaction__c.Status__c EQUAL 'Closed' — a DIFFERENT field from Stage__c — and
         closes the parent Opportunity; it is unrelated automation, not a gate on this transition.
         No validation rule exists on Transaction__c (objects/Transaction__c has no
         validationRules/ folder).

         ⚠ STILL NOT PROVEN, AND NOT PROVABLE FROM A REPO: RENDERER BEHAVIOUR. After deploying, a
         human must open a Transaction at each of Open Contract / Due Diligence / Closing Prep /
         Post-Closing / Closed Won and confirm exactly one correctly-named stage button (none at
         Closed Won), and none of the six retired highlights-panel actions, for both a
         Transaction_Stage_Actions holder and a non-holder (who should see NO stage button at any
         stage). -->
